{"schema":1,"id":"git-branches","title":"Why does a merge sometimes need a new commit?","lang":"en","sources":["https://git-scm.com/docs/git-merge/2.52.0","https://git-scm.com/docs/git-branch/2.52.0","https://learngitbranching.js.org/"],"settings":[{"id":"history","label":"Main history","default":"diverged","options":[{"value":"diverged","label":"Main makes its own commit"},{"value":"linear","label":"Main stays at the shared commit"}]}],"answer":"A merge needs a new commit when each branch has a commit the other lacks","checks":[{"question":"After M is made, stay on main and run git merge feature again. Does main move back to B, make another commit, or stay at M?","answer":"It stays at M. B is already in M’s history, so Git reports Already up to date. Main has already incorporated feature; moving main back to B would discard C from main’s history."},{"question":"After M is made, switch to feature and run git merge main, with fast-forwards allowed. New commit, fast-forward, or no change?","answer":"Fast-forward. Feature is at B, which is already one of M’s parents, while main has commits feature lacks. Git moves feature from B to M without making a commit."},{"question":"Start again with feature at B and main at M. On feature, run git merge --no-ff main. Could Git fast-forward, and what does this option ask it to do instead?","answer":"A fast-forward would be possible because B is in M’s history. --no-ff asks Git to create a merge commit anyway, with B as its first parent and M as its second. The history makes a fast-forward possible; the chosen merge policy decides whether to use it."}],"cases":[{"values":{"history":"diverged"},"name":"Main history: Main makes its own commit","duration":78.033,"paper":"#ffffff","steps":[{"step":"question","title":"Both branches moved on. Can a merge just move main to B?","line":"Predict: if the main label moved to B, which edit would main lose?","caption":"Both branches started at A, where colour.txt is blue. On feature, B made it green; on main, commit C added title.txt, Home. We have main checked out (HEAD), so the files below are C’s. A branch label names a commit; arrows lead back through its history. Could moving main to B combine the edits?","start":0,"end":20.267,"hold":0.533,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"C","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"C","merge":"none"},"files":{"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},"advanced":true,"phase":"question"},"changed":{"frame":{"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"C","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"C","merge":"none"}},"files":{"after":{"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}},"advanced":{"after":true},"phase":{"after":"question"}},"picture":"A. B. C. main. feature. HEAD: main. File. Working contents. colour.txt. blue. title.txt. Home. Arrows point from a commit to its parent.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                   ┌──────────────┐                    HEAD: main\n│                                   │   feature    │\n│                                   └──────────────┘\n│                                  ──────  B  │\n│          ╭─────╮     ────────────     │     │\n│          │  A  ◀─────                 ╰─────╯\n│          │     │     ────────────     ╭─────╮\n│          ╰─────╯                 ──────     │\n│                                       │  C  │\n│                                   ┌──────────────┐\n│                                   │    main      │\n│                                   │              │\n│                                   └──────────────┘\n│                File                                      Working contents\n│\n│              ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  colour.txt                        blue\n│\n│                 title.txt                           Home\n│\n│                           Arrows point from a commit to its parent.\n│"},{"step":"lost","title":"Answer: the Home edit. No branch would reach C","line":"B’s history is B, then A; C is not in it.","caption":"With main on B, checking out main gives green and no title.txt. B’s history is B, then A, so neither branch would contain C or the Home edit. C is still stored: moving the label does not delete the commit. To keep main’s history, following parent arrows from its new destination must still reach its old commit. A merge needs a new commit when each branch has a commit the other lacks.","start":20.267,"end":47.267,"hold":20.967,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"none"},"files":{"colour":"green","title":null},"advanced":true,"lost":["C"],"phase":"lost"},"changed":{"frame":{"before":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"C","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"C","merge":"none"},"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"none"}},"files":{"before":{"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},"after":{"colour":"green","title":null}},"phase":{"before":"question","after":"lost"},"lost":{"after":["C"]}},"picture":"A. B. C. main / feature. no branch. HEAD: main. File. Working contents. colour.txt. green. title.txt. absent. C is outside both branch histories.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                              ┌───────────────────────────┐            HEAD: main\n│                              │      main / feature       │\n│                              └───────────────────────────┘\n│                                  ──────  B  │\n│          ╭─────╮     ────────────     │     │\n│          │  A  ◀─────                 ╰─────╯\n│          │     │     ────────────     ╭─────╮\n│          ╰─────╯                 ──────     │\n│                                       │  C  │\n│                                ┌───────────────────┐\n│                                │     no branch     │\n│                                │                   │\n│                                └───────────────────┘\n│                File                                      Working contents\n│\n│              ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  colour.txt                         green\n│\n│                 title.txt                           absent\n│\n│                              C is outside both branch histories.\n│"},{"step":"merge","title":"So git merge writes M, a commit with two parents","line":"Predict: if main had never made C, would Git still need M?","caption":"git merge feature creates M with parents C and B and moves main to it. M’s files have both edits, green and Home, because the two edits touch different files. Feature stays at B, and C stays in main’s history.","start":47.267,"end":62.267,"hold":47.967,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},{"id":"M","parents":["C","B"],"colour":"green","title":"Home"}],"main":"M","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"M","merge":"commit"},"files":{"colour":"green","title":"Home"},"advanced":true,"phase":"merge"},"changed":{"frame":{"before":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"none"},"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},{"id":"M","parents":["C","B"],"colour":"green","title":"Home"}],"main":"M","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"M","merge":"commit"}},"files":{"before":{"colour":"green","title":null},"after":{"colour":"green","title":"Home"}},"lost":{"before":["C"]},"phase":{"before":"lost","after":"merge"}},"picture":"A. B. C. M. main. feature. HEAD: main. File. Working contents. colour.txt. green. title.txt. Home. M records parents C and B.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│\n│\n│\n│\n│                                   ┌──────────────┐                    HEAD: main\n│                                   │   feature    │                 ┌──────────────┐\n│                                   └──────────────┘                 │     main     │\n│                                  ──────  B  │◀──────               └──────────────┘\n│          ╭─────╮     ────────────     │     │       ─────────────       ╭─────╮\n│          │  A  ◀─────                 ╰─────╯                    ───────│  M  │\n│          │     │     ────────────     ╭─────╮       ─────────────       │     │\n│          ╰─────╯                 ──────     │◀──────                    ╰─────╯\n│                                       │  C  │\n│                                       ╰─────╯\n│\n│\n│\n│                File                                      Working contents\n│\n│              ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n│                  colour.txt                         green\n│\n│                 title.txt                           Home\n│\n│                                  M records parents C and B.\n│"},{"step":"countercase","title":"Answer: no. Without C, main just moves to B","line":"A is in B’s history, so moving main to B loses nothing.","caption":"Here main never made C and still points at A, B’s parent. With fast-forwards allowed, git merge feature moves main to B; colour.txt turns green. --no-ff would request a merge commit even here: that is a policy choice, not a missing edit.","start":62.267,"end":78.033,"hold":62.967,"state":{"frame":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"fast-forward"},"files":{"colour":"green","title":null},"advanced":false,"phase":"countercase"},"changed":{"frame":{"before":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null},{"id":"C","parents":["A"],"colour":"blue","title":"Home"},{"id":"M","parents":["C","B"],"colour":"green","title":"Home"}],"main":"M","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"M","merge":"commit"},"after":{"commits":[{"id":"A","parents":[],"colour":"blue","title":null},{"id":"B","parents":["A"],"colour":"green","title":null}],"main":"B","feature":"B","head":"main","current":"B","merge":"fast-forward"}},"files":{"before":{"colour":"green","title":"Home"},"after":{"colour":"green","title":null}},"advanced":{"before":true,"after":false},"phase":{"before":"merge","after":"countercase"}},"picture":"A. B. main / feature. HEAD: main. File. Working contents. colour.txt. green. title.txt. absent. main moves to existing commit B.","drawing":"┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────